# Brand-named cards depict the brand

Hard rule for diana’s dashboard (`/Users/diana/my-dashboard`) card photos.

## When a card is named after a brand

If Diana names a **brand** on a card (e.g. **smile set**, Medicube, Bellami, Stasis):

- The card photo must **read as that brand** — packaging, product, or logo with the **brand name visible** when that’s how the product is recognized
- Do **not** substitute a generic category still-life (generic clear aligners with no Smile Set marking, anonymous serum bottle, etc.)

## Still forbidden

- Other people’s **faces**
- Other people’s **personal names** (researchers, authors, strangers)
- Brand names she did **not** put on the card

## Allowed

- The brand she wrote on the card (Smile Set, etc.)
- Her own name / brand when she asks

## Examples

- **smile set** → Smile Set aligners / kit with “Smile Set” visible — not unlabeled trays
- **Medicube** → Medicube product packaging — not a blank skincare bottle
